  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN. Each AiA_iAi​ equals 1,2,1, 2, 1,2, or 333.\n\nYou can perform the following operation on AAA:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1&lt;i&lt;N1 \\lt i \\lt N1&lt;i&lt;N) such that Ai−1+Ai+1=4A_{i-1} + A_{i+1} = 4Ai−1​+Ai+1​=4.\nThen, replace AiA_iAi​ with 4−Ai4 - A_i4−Ai​.\nYou may perform this operation however many times you like (including zero).\n\nFind the **minimum** possible sum of AAA in the end.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, denoting the length of AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the initial elements of AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible sum of AAA after performing several operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "3≤N≤3⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^53≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤31 \\leq A_i \\leq 31≤Ai​≤3",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5\n1 2 3 3 2\n5\n3 2 3 2 3\n6\n1 3 3 2 3 3",
        "output": "11\n11\n13",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: It's best to not perform any operations. The answer is the sum of AAA, which is 111111.\nTest case 222: Choose i=3i = 3i=3. Since A2+A4=4A_{2} + A_4 = 4A2​+A4​=4, we can operate on A3A_3A3​ and turn it into 4−A3=14 - A_3 = 14−A3​=1. The array is now [3,2,1,2,3][3, 2, 1, 2, 3][3,2,1,2,3], with a sum of 111111. This is optimal.\nTest case 333: Operate on i=2i = 2i=2 to obtain [1,1,3,2,3,3][1, 1, 3, 2, 3, 3][1,1,3,2,3,3] with a sum of 131313."
      }
    ]
  },
